   "id": "co_north_face_submitted_as_normal_route",
   "area_id": "co_jagged_mountain",
   "name": "North Face (submitted as Normal Route)",
   "grade": "5.2",
   "discipline": "alpine",
   "overview": "Starts just right of the big snowy gully. Wet ledges lead to a 20-foot corner of about 5.5, but an easier way cuts left on an angling ramp toward the gully (possibly the 4th class ramp, grimy and wet). Grass leads up to the foot of the upper cliffs; go right, passing behind a little block, cross a gully top, and follow ledges to the rock step under the notch. A short 5.2 section has little gear but a slung block anchor. From the notch work left across exposed ledges, roping up for the corner step that overlooks a drop; an easy chimney and one tricky move reach the summit. Descend via an 8-foot slot and rappel the rock step. Two summit bolts allow a two-rope rappel north.",
